<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Republican Party (Brazil)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">founded 1869</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Republican Party</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Republican Party of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> was a political movement founded in 1869 that campaigned for the replacement of the monarchy with a republic. Growing steadily through the 1880s, it attracted much of the landowning elite of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sao-paulo">São Paulo</a> and offered an organised political alternative to imperial rule. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a> identify it as one of the forces that made the monarchy's overthrow in 1889 possible.</p></div>
